# oracle — one full market in TRADER mode, from open to resolution.
#
# Frame budget: a market is TICKS(26) * TICKFRAMES(48) = 1248 frames, plus the
# ~12 to clear the title. Run to ~1330 to catch the endcard settling.
#
#   node tools/make-gif.js oracle --recipe 01-one-market
#
# What the clip is FOR: the two markers on the bar. The green fill is what the
# crowd will sell you; the yellow caret is what you think once your private
# sources have spoken, and the shaded strip between them is the only money in
# the cart. Watch the caret jump the moment a source whispers, then watch the
# crowd's own evidence drag the price toward it (or not — sometimes the source
# was the tavern drunk).
#
# Nothing here is scripted. The chart line is the residue of simulated order
# flow, so the shape differs per seed; the trades below are only timed to sit
# on either side of a couple of tip arrivals so the position swings visibly.
# frames 1330
# fps 30
down 10 ENTER
up 12 ENTER
down 120 Z
up 122 Z
down 300 Z
up 302 Z
down 500 X
up 502 X
down 800 Z
up 802 Z
down 1000 X
up 1002 X
